            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "The biologic redistribution of the limiting nutrients, NO3 and PO4, is controlled by the rules given in Figure 3. For each box that reaches the sea surface a nutrient residence time is assigned. These times refer to the removal of the limiting nutrients from the box to an underlying box as falling organic debris (nutrient recycling within a given box is not included).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "PANDORA",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "silica cycle scheme",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "The silica cycle is handled in the same manner as the limiting nutrient cycle. However, a different set of biologic residence times and destruction percentages is needed to reproduce the observed silica distribution (Fig 4).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
